.page volume 1 show or set the master volume

# SYNOPSIS
*volume* [_PERCENT_ | *+*_PERCENT_ | *-*_PERCENT_ | *mute* | *unmute* | *toggle* | _LEFT_ _RIGHT_]

# DESCRIPTION
`volume` shows or changes the master volume of the machine: the level applied to everything that plays through `/dev/audio`, after the mixer has added the programs together. Without arguments it prints the current setting. The scale is 0 to 100 and follows the ear (50 is a quarter of the amplitude of 100, not half), so it feels even all the way down.

The setting lives in the kernel and lasts until the machine is restarted; it starts at 60. Muting keeps the volume and silences the output until `unmute`.

# OPTIONS
@ _PERCENT_
    Set both channels to this volume.
@ *+*_PERCENT_, *-*_PERCENT_
    Raise or lower both channels, within 0 to 100.
@ _LEFT_ _RIGHT_
    Set the channels separately.
@ *mute*, *unmute*, *toggle*
    Silence the output, bring it back, or flip between the two.

# EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 if there is no sound device or it is not allowed; 2 for a usage error.

# EXAMPLES
    volume
    volume 35
    volume -10
    volume toggle

# SEE ALSO
beep(1), play(1), audio(7)
